{
 "encounter_id": "00673",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Doctor, I need help, now. It's my back, my right side. I can't stay still, I'm pacing, I can't sit."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can see how uncomfortable you are. Let's get you sorted. When did it start?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About two hours ago. Came out of nowhere. It comes in waves, then I think it's gone, and then it's worse."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where does it go?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "From the back round to the front, down towards my groin. It's the worst pain of my life, honestly. I'd say it's severe."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had this before?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, I've had stones. One, two years ago, and they blasted it with a lithotripsy, I think that's the word."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That helps. Have you been feeling feverish?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever. No shivers. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you have any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Penicillin, I come out in a rash. Doctor, please, can I have something for the pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, we're going to sort that out right now. Pulse and the rest first, so I'm safe. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on, quickly. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 98, blood pressure 156 over 92, temperature 36.9, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 18.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that okay? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's what I'd expect with pain like yours. I'm going to press on your back and tummy. Tell me when it's sore. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "There! Right there! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very tender over the right loin, but your tummy is soft, with no guarding."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What is it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Judging by the pain, how it comes in waves and goes to the groin, and your history, this looks most like a kidney stone."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. I knew it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'm going to give you diclofenac, 75 mg, by injection, now, for kidney stone pain. It acts quickly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thank God. Will it hurt? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A small jab in the thigh, that's all. Nurse will help. And I'd like to arrange a CT scan of your kidneys and bladder, to see the stone's size and where it sits."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Do I need that? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, I want to rule out a blockage. And a urine test too, to check for infection and blood."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. Do what you need. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Drink plenty of water, and we'll strain your urine to catch the stone, in case we can analyse it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Strain? Lovely. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It helps to know what type it is. If the pain isn't controlled within an hour, or you develop a fever, tell the nurse straight away and we'll review you."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
